          "q": "SLO LQ 1: Comprehensive Analysis of Rutherford vs. Bohr Atomic Models: Compare experimental foundations, postulates, energy states, and spectrum explanations in detailed tabular format.",
          "ans": "1. Experimental Basis: Rutherford used alpha scattering on gold foil (classical physics); Bohr used Hydrogen emission line spectrum (Planck's quantum theory).\n2. Electron Trajectory: Rutherford proposed unquantized planetary circular paths; Bohr established quantized circular orbits where mvr = nh / 2π.\n3. Energy Emission: Rutherford predicted continuous emission and atomic collapse; Bohr established stationary non-radiating states where energy ΔE = hν is emitted only during quantum jumps.\n4. Atomic Spectrum: Rutherford predicted continuous spectrum; Bohr successfully derived and explained discrete hydrogen line spectrum series (Lyman, Balmer, Paschen).\n5. Atomic Stability: Rutherford model failed to explain stability; Bohr model completely resolved atomic stability."
