          "q": "1. (SLO) Comprehensive Analysis: Compare the three states of matter (solid, liquid, gas) in terms of particle arrangement, intermolecular forces, kinetic energy, density, compressibility, and diffusion.",
          "ans": "1. Particle Arrangement:\n• Solid: Tightly packed in fixed, orderly geometric crystal lattice.\n• Liquid: Closely packed but disorderly with particles able to slide over one another.\n• Gas: Widely separated with vast intermolecular empty spaces (>99% empty volume).\n\n2. Intermolecular Forces:\n• Solid: Extremely strong cohesive forces keeping particles at mean positions.\n• Liquid: Moderate forces strong enough to maintain fixed volume but allow fluidity.\n• Gas: Negligible/weak intermolecular forces.\n\n3. Molecular Motion & Kinetic Energy:\n• Solid: Low kinetic energy; only vibrational motion about mean positions.\n• Liquid: Moderate kinetic energy; translational, rotational, and vibrational motions.\n• Gas: High kinetic energy; rapid, continuous, random translational motion in all directions.\n\n4. Density:\n• Solid: Highest density (e.g. solid O2 = 1.42 g/cm^3).\n• Liquid: High density (e.g. liquid O2 = 1.149 g/cm^3; water = 1.00 g/cm^3).\n• Gas: Extremely low density (e.g. gaseous O2 = 0.00142 g/cm^3 at STP).\n\n5. Compressibility:\n• Solid: Incompressible (no empty spaces between particles).\n• Liquid: Almost negligible compressibility.\n• Gas: Highly compressible (large empty spaces easily reduced under pressure).\n\n6. Diffusion Rate:\n• Solid: Negligible / extremely slow.\n• Liquid: Moderate / slow.\n• Gas: Very rapid and spontaneous forming homogeneous mixtures."
