            "ans": "**Given:**\n- $[N_2] = 0.602 \\text{ mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3}$\n- $[H_2] = 0.420 \\text{ mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3}$\n- $[NH_3] = 0.113 \\text{ mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3}$\n- Reaction: $N_2(g) + 3H_2(g) \\rightleftharpoons 2NH_3(g)$\n\n**Required:**\n- Equilibrium Constant ($K_c$)\n\n**Formula:**\n$$K_c = \\frac{[NH_3]^2}{[N_2][H_2]^3}$$\n\n**Calculation:**\n$$[NH_3]^2 = (0.113)^2 = 0.012769$$\n$$[H_2]^3 = (0.420)^3 = 0.074088$$\n$$[N_2][H_2]^3 = 0.602 \\times 0.074088 = 0.044601$$\n$$K_c = \\frac{0.012769}{0.044601} \\approx 0.286$$\n\n**Units of Kc:**\n$$\\frac{(\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3})^2}{(\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3})(\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3})^3} = \\text{mol}^{-2}\\cdot\\text{dm}^6$$\n\n**Final Answer:** $K_c = 0.286 \\text{ mol}^{-2}\\cdot\\text{dm}^6$"
