            "ans": "**Given:**\n- $[SO_2] = 1.50 \\text{ mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3}$\n- $[O_2] = 1.25 \\text{ mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3}$\n- $[SO_3] = 3.50 \\text{ mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3}$\n- Balanced Equation: $2SO_2(g) + O_2(g) \\rightleftharpoons 2SO_3(g)$\n\n**Required:**\n- Equilibrium Constant ($K_c$)\n\n**Formula:**\n$$K_c = \\frac{[SO_3]^2}{[SO_2]^2[O_2]}$$\n\n**Calculation:**\n$$[SO_3]^2 = (3.50)^2 = 12.25$$\n$$[SO_2]^2 = (1.50)^2 = 2.25$$\n$$[SO_2]^2[O_2] = 2.25 \\times 1.25 = 2.8125$$\n$$K_c = \\frac{12.25}{2.8125} \\approx 4.36$$\n\n**Units of Kc:**\n$$\\frac{(\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3})^2}{(\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3})^2(\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3})} = \\text{mol}^{-1}\\cdot\\text{dm}^3$$\n\n**Final Answer:** $K_c = 4.36 \\text{ mol}^{-1}\\cdot\\text{dm}^3$"
