          {
            "q": "5. (a) Kc expression for a reaction is given below: Kc = [Cl₂]² [H₂O]² / ([HCl]⁴ [O₂]). For this reaction write: (i) Reactants and products, (ii) Balanced chemical equation, (iii) Derive the units of Kc. (b) Explain the importance of equilibrium constant, support your answer with examples and reasons.",
            "ans": "**(a) Analysis of the Given $K_c$ Expression:**\n$$K_c = \\frac{[Cl_2]^2 [H_2O]^2}{[HCl]^4 [O_2]}$$\n\n1. **Reactants and Products:**\n   - Denominator represents reactants: Hydrogen chloride ($HCl$) and Oxygen ($O_2$).\n   - Numerator represents products: Chlorine gas ($Cl_2$) and Water vapour ($H_2O$).\n\n2. **Balanced Chemical Equation:**\n   $$4HCl(g) + O_2(g) \\rightleftharpoons 2Cl_2(g) + 2H_2O(g)$$\n\n3. **Derivation of Units of $K_c$:**\n   $$K_c = \\frac{(\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3})^2 \\cdot (\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3})^2}{(\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3})^4 \\cdot (\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3})} = \\frac{(\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3})^4}{(\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3})^5} = \\frac{1}{\\text{mol}\\cdot\\text{dm}^{-3}} = \\text{mol}^{-1}\\cdot\\text{dm}^3$$\n\n**(b) Importance of Equilibrium Constant:**\n1. **Predicting Direction:** Comparing $Q_c$ with $K_c$ tells chemists whether forward or reverse reaction is favored at any instant.\n2. **Predicting Extent / Yield:** Tells industrial chemists whether a reaction will give high product yield ($K_c$ large) or negligible product ($K_c$ small).\n3. **Optimizing Industrial Processes:** In Haber's process for ammonia and Contact process for sulphuric acid, knowledge of $K_c$ and temperature dependence enables engineers to select temperatures that maximize product yield while maintaining acceptable reaction rates."
          }
