              "desc": "Salts play indispensable roles in our daily lives, agriculture, medicine, and industrial manufacturing:\n\n1. **Sodium Chloride ($NaCl$ - Common Table Salt):**\n- Essential dietary mineral for maintaining electrolyte balance and nerve impulses.\n- Used for preserving fish, meat, and pickles.\n- Industrial raw material for making caustic soda ($NaOH$), soda ash ($Na_2CO_3$), baking soda ($NaHCO_3$), chlorine, and hydrochloric acid.\n\n2. **Sodium Carbonate ($Na_2CO_3\\cdot 10H_2O$ - Washing Soda):**\n- Used for domestic laundry washing and softening permanent hard water.\n- Manufacturing glass, soap, paper, and chemicals.\n\n3. **Sodium Bicarbonate ($NaHCO_3$ - Baking Soda):**\n- Used as baking powder in cakes, breads, and confectionery (releases $CO_2$ gas on heating).\n- Antacid medicine to neutralize excess gastric acidity.\n- Active charge in soda-acid fire extinguishers.\n\n4. **Copper Sulphate ($CuSO_4\\cdot 5H_2O$ - Blue Vitriol):**\n- Agricultural fungicide (Bordeaux mixture) to kill fungal blights on grape vines and fruit trees.\n- Used in electroplating and dyeing.\n\n5. **Calcium Sulphate ($CaSO_4\\cdot 2H_2O$ - Gypsum & Plaster of Paris):**\n- Gypsum is added to cement to retard flash setting.\n- Plaster of Paris ($CaSO_4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}H_2O$) is used for setting fractured bones, making dental casts, statues, and decorative ceilings.",
