              "name": "Physical and Chemical Properties of Alkanes",
              "desc": "**A. Physical Properties:**\n- First four members ($C_1$ to $C_4$: methane to butane) are colourless, odourless gases.\n- Next members ($C_5$ to $C_{17}$) are colourless liquids.\n- Higher members ($C_{18}$ upwards) are waxy solids.\n- Non-polar, insoluble in water, but soluble in non-polar organic solvents (benzene, ether, $CCl_4$).\n- Melting and boiling points increase systematically with increasing molecular mass.\n\n**B. Chemical Reactions:**\nBecause of strong $\\sigma$-bonds, alkanes are inert to acids, alkalis, and oxidizing agents, but undergo two characteristic reactions:\n\n1. **Combustion (Burning in Air):**\n- *Complete Combustion (Excess Oxygen):* Burns with a clean, blue non-luminous flame producing $CO_2$, $H_2O$, and huge heat energy:\n$$CH_4(g) + 2O_2(g) \\rightarrow CO_2(g) + 2H_2O(g) + 890\\text{ kJ/mol}$$\n- *Incomplete Combustion (Limited Oxygen):* Produces highly poisonous carbon monoxide gas ($CO$) and carbon black (soot):\n$$3CH_4(g) + 4O_2(g) \\rightarrow 2CO(g) + C(s) + 6H_2O(g)$$\n\n2. **Halogenation (Substitution Reaction):**\nAlkanes react with halogens in the presence of **diffused sunlight or UV light** via a series of four successive substitution steps where hydrogen atoms are successively replaced by chlorine atoms:\n- Step 1: $CH_4 + Cl_2 \\xrightarrow{\\text{diffused sunlight}} CH_3Cl + HCl$ (Chloromethane / Methyl chloride)\n- Step 2: $CH_3Cl + Cl_2 \\xrightarrow{h\\nu} CH_2Cl_2 + HCl$ (Dichloromethane / Methylene chloride)\n- Step 3: $CH_2Cl_2 + Cl_2 \\xrightarrow{h\\nu} CHCl_3 + HCl$ (Trichloromethane / Chloroform)\n- Step 4: $CHCl_3 + Cl_2 \\xrightarrow{h\\nu} CCl_4 + HCl$ (Tetrachloromethane / Carbon tetrachloride)\n*(Note: In direct bright sunlight, an explosive reaction occurs: $CH_4 + 2Cl_2 \\xrightarrow{\\text{direct sunlight}} C + 4HCl$).*",
