              "name": "Sources and Biological Uses of Carbohydrates",
              "desc": "**Natural Sources:**\n- Monosaccharides: Grapes, honey, apples, dates, figs, sweet fruits.\n- Disaccharides: Sugarcane, sugar beet (sucrose); sprouted barley (maltose); cow/buffalo milk (lactose).\n- Polysaccharides: Grains (wheat, barley, maize, rice), potatoes (starch); cotton, wood pulp, flax (cellulose).\n\n**Biological and Industrial Uses:**\n1. **Primary Energy Source:** Glucose is the primary cellular fuel oxidized during cellular respiration to yield ATP energy: $C_6H_{12}O_6 + 6O_2 \\rightarrow 6CO_2 + 6H_2O + 2820\\text{ kJ}$.\n2. **Energy Storage:** Plants store energy as starch; animals store energy as glycogen in liver and muscles.\n3. **Structural Support:** Cellulose provides rigid structural frameworks for plant cell walls.\n4. **Industrial Applications:** Starch is used in paper sizing, adhesives, and textiles; cellulose is used to manufacture paper, cellophane, rayon, and explosives (gun cotton).",
