              "num": "13.5.2",
              "name": "Sources, Functions and Deficiency Diseases of Key Vitamins",
              "desc": "1. **Vitamin A (Retinol - Fat-Soluble):**\n- *Sources:* Carrots, spinach, fish liver oil, egg yolk, butter, yellow fruits (papaya, mango).\n- *Biological Role:* Component of rhodopsin pigment in retina needed for vision in dim light; maintains healthy epithelial tissues.\n- *Deficiency Disease:* **Night Blindness (Nyctalopia)**, Xerophthalmia (dry, keratinized cornea).\n\n2. **Vitamin D (Calciferol - Fat-Soluble):**\n- *Sources:* Sunlight exposure (skin synthesizes it from cholesterol), cod liver oil, fortified milk, eggs.\n- *Biological Role:* Facilitates calcium and phosphorus absorption from intestine for bone and tooth mineralization.\n- *Deficiency Disease:* **Rickets** in growing children (soft, bent bowlegs); **Osteomalacia** in adults (soft, brittle bones).\n\n3. **Vitamin E (Tocopherol - Fat-Soluble):**\n- *Sources:* Vegetable oils, wheat germ, nuts, seeds, leafy greens.\n- *Biological Role:* Potent antioxidant protecting cell membranes from free radical damage.\n- *Deficiency Disease:* Hemolytic anemia, neurological deficits, muscle weakness.\n\n4. **Vitamin K (Phylloquinone - Fat-Soluble):**\n- *Sources:* Green leafy vegetables (cabbage, spinach), synthesized by gut flora bacteria.\n- *Biological Role:* Essential for hepatic synthesis of prothrombin and blood clotting factors.\n- *Deficiency Disease:* **Hemorrhagic disease (prolonged bleeding)**, failure of blood to clot.\n\n5. **Vitamin B-Complex (Water-Soluble):**\n- *Sources:* Whole grains, yeast, liver, pulses, dairy.\n- *Deficiency Diseases:* Vitamin B₁ (Thiamine) deficiency causes **Beriberi** (nerve and heart failure); Vitamin B₃ (Niacin) deficiency causes **Pellagra** (diarrhea, dermatitis, dementia).\n\n6. **Vitamin C (Ascorbic Acid - Water-Soluble):**\n- *Sources:* Fresh citrus fruits (oranges, lemons, grapefruits), amla, tomatoes, green peppers.\n- *Biological Role:* Synthesis of collagen in connective tissues, wound healing, antioxidant immune defense.\n- *Deficiency Disease:* **Scurvy** (bleeding swollen gums, loose teeth, poor wound healing).",
