              "desc": "**Air Pollutant:** Any harmful chemical substance or particulate matter introduced into the air in concentrations that endanger human health, animals, vegetation, or physical materials.\n\n**Two Main Categories of Air Pollutants:**\n\n1. **Primary Pollutants:**\nHarmful gases or substances emitted **directly** into the atmosphere from identifiable natural or anthropogenic sources:\n- **Carbon Monoxide ($CO$):** Highly toxic, colourless, odourless gas produced by the **incomplete combustion** of fossil fuels (automobiles, coal, wood, cigarettes).\n- **Carbon Dioxide ($CO_2$):** Released by complete combustion of fossil fuels, forest fires, and cement factories; primary greenhouse gas.\n- **Sulphur Dioxide ($SO_2$):** Sharp pungent gas emitted by burning sulphur-containing coal and heavy oil in power stations, and copper/lead smelting.\n- **Oxides of Nitrogen ($NO$ and $NO_2$, together called $NO_x$):** Formed in automobile combustion engines and thermal power plants when nitrogen and oxygen combine at high combustion temperatures ($>1200^\\circ\\text{C}$).\n- **Unburnt Hydrocarbons ($CH_4, C_2H_4$):** Emitted from vehicle exhausts and petroleum refineries.\n- **Particulate Matter (PM):** Soot, smoke, fly ash, dust, and lead aerosols.\n\n2. **Secondary Pollutants:**\nHarmful pollutants that are **not emitted directly**, but are formed in the atmosphere through **chemical and photochemical reactions** between primary pollutants and normal atmospheric gases (water vapour, oxygen, sunlight):\n- **Sulphuric Acid ($H_2SO_4$):** Formed when primary $SO_2$ is oxidized to $SO_3$ and dissolves in atmospheric moisture.\n- **Nitric Acid ($HNO_3$):** Formed when primary $NO_2$ reacts with atmospheric hydroxyl radicals and moisture.\n- **Carbonic Acid ($H_2CO_3$):** Dissolution of $CO_2$ in cloud droplets.\n- **Tropospheric (Ground-Level) Ozone ($O_3$):** Formed by photochemical reactions between $NO_x$ and hydrocarbons in sunlight.\n- **Peroxyacyl Nitrates (PAN):** Powerful eye-irritating component of photochemical smog.",
