              "name": "Harmful Effects of Acid Rain",
              "desc": "Acid rain inflicts severe multi-dimensional ecological, human, and economic damage:\n\n1. **Destruction of Aquatic Ecosystems:**\n- When acid rain flows into lakes, streams, and rivers, water pH drops below $5.0$.\n- Toxic aluminium ions ($Al^{3+}$) are leached from soil into waterways, which asphyxiate fish by precipitating on their gills and blocking oxygen exchange.\n- Fish eggs fail to hatch at pH < 5.0, resulting in completely 'dead', sterile lakes.\n\n2. **Defoliation and Forest Damage:**\n- Acid rain erodes the waxy protective cuticle layer on leaves and needles of trees, increasing transpiration and causing leaf necrosis.\n- Leaches vital mineral nutrients (Calcium $Ca^{2+}$, Magnesium $Mg^{2+}$, Potassium $K^+$) deep out of topsoil, starving plant roots.\n\n3. **Damage to Historical Buildings and Statues (Stone Cancer):**\n- Acid rain attacks building materials containing calcium carbonate (marble, limestone, dolomite):\n  $$CaCO_3(s) + H_2SO_4(aq) \\rightarrow CaSO_4(s) + H_2O(l) + CO_2(g) \\uparrow$$\n- Insoluble calcium sulphate ($CaSO_4$, gypsum) flakes away, causing pitting, discolouration, and loss of structural details on world heritage monuments (e.g. Taj Mahal in Agra).\n\n4. **Corrosion of Metals:**\n- Rapidly corrodes steel bridges, iron railway tracks, pipelines, and automobile sheet metal: $Fe + H_2SO_4 \\rightarrow FeSO_4 + H_2 \\uparrow$.\n\n5. **Human Health Hazards:**\n- Fine sulphate and nitrate aerosols penetrate deep into human lungs, aggravating chronic bronchitis, asthma, and cardiopulmonary diseases.\n- Leaches heavy metals ($Pb, Cu, Cd$) from household plumbing pipes into drinking water, causing toxic poisoning.",
              "sciNote": "To protect historical marble monuments like the Taj Mahal, governments establish 'Clean Air Zones' prohibiting coal-fired factories and diesel vehicles within a 50 km radius.",
