              "desc": "Water is the most abundant natural substance on Earth, covering approximately **$71\\%$ of the planetary surface**.\n\n**Distribution of Earth's Water:**\n- **Oceans and Seas:** $97.2\\%$ — Saline water unfit for direct human consumption or agriculture without desalination.\n- **Glaciers and Polar Ice Caps:** $2.15\\%$ — Locked in polar ice sheets (Greenland, Antarctica) and high mountain glaciers.\n- **Fresh Groundwater:** $0.62\\%$ — Aquifers tapped by tube-wells and springs.\n- **Surface Freshwater (Lakes, Rivers, Streams):** Only about **$0.01\\%$** of total planetary water, yet sustains all terrestrial ecosystems, human civilization, and agriculture.\n\n**Water in Living Organisms:**\n- Human body weight is approximately **$60–70\\%$ water**.\n- Human blood plasma consists of **$90–92\\%$ water**.\n- Plant tissues (such as cucumber, watermelon, and tomatoes) consist of **$90–95\\%$ water**.",
