              "desc": "Hard water causes substantial economic and technical problems in daily life and heavy industry:\n1. **Wastage of Soap:** Consumes enormous amounts of soap forming useless, greasy scum before any cleaning lather develops.\n2. **Boiler Scale Formation:** When hard water is heated in industrial steam boilers, water heaters, and steam pipes, dissolved salts precipitate out as a hard, rock-like crust called **boiler scale** (composed of $CaCO_3, CaSO_4, Mg(OH)_2$):\n   - *Fuel Inefficiency:* Boiler scale is an extremely poor conductor of heat, requiring up to $30–50\\%$ more fuel to produce steam.\n   - *Boiler Explosions:* Overheating of scaled metal causes boiler walls to weaken and rupture violently under high steam pressure.\n3. **Clogging of Plumbing Pipes:** Scale buildup narrows household water pipes, reducing flow and blocking valves.\n4. **Unsuitable for Textile & Dyeing Industries:** Scum damages fabrics, interferes with dye adherence, and causes streaks and spots on finished garments.\n5. **Digestive Disorders:** Prolonged consumption of excessively hard water can cause stomach irritation and contributes to the formation of calcium oxalate kidney stones.",
