              "name": "Types and Sources of Water Pollutants",
              "desc": "**Water Pollution:** Any physical, chemical, or biological alteration in water quality that makes it harmful or unfit for humans, animals, aquatic life, or agriculture.\n\n**Three Major Sources of Water Pollution:**\n\n1. **Industrial Wastes (Effluents):**\nFactories (textile mills, tanneries, chemical plants, sugar mills, metal plating) discharge millions of liters of untreated toxic liquid wastes into rivers and canals:\n- *Heavy Metal Toxins:* Lead ($Pb$), Cadmium ($Cd$), Mercury ($Hg$), Chromium ($Cr$), and Arsenic ($As$). These are non-biodegradable and bioaccumulate up the food chain, causing kidney failure, brain damage, and cancer (e.g. Minamata disease from mercury; Itai-itai disease from cadmium).\n- *Acids and Alkalis:* Drastically alter the pH of receiving water bodies, exterminating aquatic organisms.\n- *Organic Compounds:* Dyes, phenols, aromatic solvents that impart dark colour, offensive odours, and carcinogenicity.\n\n2. **Domestic Sewage and Household Wastes:**\nUntreated municipal wastewater from kitchens, toilets, and bathrooms containing human excreta, soaps, food residues, and **synthetic detergents**:\n- *Pathogens:* Sewage carries disease-causing viruses, bacteria, and protozoa into municipal drinking supplies.\n- *Detergents:* Contain non-biodegradable alkyl benzene sulphonates and **polyphosphate builders** that generate persistent foam on water surfaces, preventing atmospheric oxygen dissolution.\n\n3. **Agricultural Runoff (Fertilizers and Pesticides):**\n- *Chemical Fertilizers:* Synthetic urea, ammonium sulphate, and superphosphate are washed by rain from fields into rivers and ponds.\n- *Pesticides & Herbicides:* Toxic organochlorines (DDT) and organophosphates applied to crops seep into underground aquifers and surface runoff, poisoning aquatic fauna.",
