              "num": "16.3.2",
              "name": "Percentage of Nitrogen in Urea and Industrial Uses",
              "desc": "**Calculation of Percentage of Nitrogen in Urea:**\n- Chemical Formula of Urea: $NH_2CONH_2$ or $CH_4N_2O$\n- Atomic masses: $C = 12, H = 1, N = 14, O = 16$\n- **Molar Mass of Urea:**\n  $$\\text{Molar Mass} = 12 + 16 + 2(14) + 4(1) = 12 + 16 + 28 + 4 = 60\\text{ g/mol}$$\n- Mass of Nitrogen in 1 mole of urea = $2 \\times 14 = 28\\text{ g}$\n- **Percentage of Nitrogen:**\n  $$\\%\\text{ Nitrogen} = \\frac{\\text{Mass of Nitrogen in Formula}}{\\text{Molar Mass of Urea}} \\times 100 = \\frac{28}{60} \\times 100 = 46.666...\\% \\approx \\mathbf{46.67\\%}$$\n\n**Uses of Urea:**\n1. **Agricultural Fertilizer:** Supplies $46.67\\%$ assimilable nitrogen to plants, promoting rapid green vegetative foliage growth and higher crop yields (wheat, rice, sugarcane, cotton).\n2. **Manufacture of Synthetic Resins and Plastics:** Reacted with formaldehyde to produce **urea-formaldehyde resins**, used in particle boards, plywood adhesives, laminates, and unbreakable tableware.\n3. **Pharmaceuticals:** Raw material for synthesizing sedatives and sleeping pills (barbiturates).\n4. **Animal Feed Supplement:** Added in small regulated doses to ruminant animal feed as a non-protein nitrogen supplement for bacterial protein synthesis.",
              "sciNote": "Urea is the chief solid nitrogenous metabolic waste product excreted in human urine (averaging ~25–30 grams of urea excreted per adult per day).",
