              "num": "16.4.2",
              "name": "Major Fractions of Petroleum and Their Uses",
              "desc": "The primary fractions obtained from the fractional distillation of crude oil in order of increasing boiling points are:\n\n1. **Petroleum Gas (Refinery Gas):**\n- *Boiling Point:* Below $20^\\circ\\text{C}$\n- *Carbon Range:* $C_1$ to $C_4$ ($CH_4, C_2H_6, C_3H_8, C_4H_{10}$)\n- *Uses:* Liquefied under pressure as LPG (Liquefied Petroleum Gas) for domestic cooking and automotive fuel; petrochemical feedstock.\n\n2. **Petroleum Ether / Ligroin:**\n- *Boiling Point:* $20–60^\\circ\\text{C}$ / $60–100^\\circ\\text{C}$\n- *Carbon Range:* $C_5$ to $C_7$\n- *Uses:* Laboratory and industrial solvent for non-polar oils and fats; dry cleaning.\n\n3. **Gasoline (Petrol):**\n- *Boiling Point:* $40–200^\\circ\\text{C}$\n- *Carbon Range:* $C_6$ to $C_{10}$\n- *Uses:* Motor fuel for passenger cars, motorcycles, and light internal combustion engines.\n\n4. **Kerosene Oil (Paraffin Oil):**\n- *Boiling Point:* $175–275^\\circ\\text{C}$\n- *Carbon Range:* $C_{10}$ to $C_{14}$\n- *Uses:* Aviation jet turbine fuel (aviation kerosene); domestic heating and cooking stoves.\n\n5. **Diesel Oil (Gas Oil):**\n- *Boiling Point:* $250–350^\\circ\\text{C}$\n- *Carbon Range:* $C_{14}$ to $C_{18}$\n- *Uses:* Heavy transport fuel for buses, trucks, tractors, railway diesel locomotives, and electricity generators.\n\n6. **Lubricating Oils and Greases:**\n- *Boiling Point:* $350–400^\\circ\\text{C}$\n- *Carbon Range:* $C_{18}$ to $C_{20}$\n- *Uses:* Lubrication of machinery and automotive engine parts to reduce friction and wear.\n\n7. **Paraffin Wax:**\n- *Carbon Range:* $C_{20}$ to $C_{30}$\n- *Uses:* Candles, shoe polish, waterproof waxed paper, petroleum jelly (Vaseline).\n\n8. **Asphalt / Bitumen (Residue):**\n- *Boiling Point:* Non-volatile residue ($>400^\\circ\\text{C}$)\n- *Carbon Range:* Above $C_{30}$\n- *Uses:* Surfacing and paving tarmac roads; roof waterproofing.",
              "sciNote": "Cracking (pyrolysis) is used in refineries to break heavy, low-value fuel oil fractions into high-demand lighter gasoline fractions.",
